#[repr(C)]
pub struct PacketHeader {
    pub tag: u8,
    pub len: u32,
    pub flags: u16,
}

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn packet_header_size() -> usize {
    std::mem::size_of::<PacketHeader>()
}
```

`#[repr(C)]` guarantees the struct follows the C ABI layout: fields are placed in declaration order with padding inserted to satisfy each field's natural alignment, and the overall struct size is rounded up to a multiple of the largest field alignment (4 bytes here). On any target where the C compiler uses the same alignment rules (which is the standard C behavior), the resulting layout — field offsets `0`, `4`, `8` and total size `12` — will be identical to the C struct.
